1
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:08,060
All right, Raj has played his phantom warlord card,

2
00:00:08,130 --> 00:00:12,900
And I am going to back him up with my strangling vines.

3
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:16,440
Choke on that, sucka.

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:21,340
Okay, well, then I'll just cut your vines with my ruby sword.

5
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:25,280
That's right, I did it. I cut 'em.

6
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,100
I have a question.

7
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:33,850
Warlord beats troll, troll beats elf,

8
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:35,190
Elf beats water sprite,

9
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:38,730
And basically everything beats enchanted bunny.

10
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:40,760
Unless you have the carrot powder.

11
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:43,900
Okay, I've got another question.

12
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:45,920
When does this get fun?

13
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:47,870
Are we going to talk

14
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:50,820
Or are we going to play "mystic warriors of ka-ah"?

15
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:53,120
Just play a potion card.

16
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:54,590
Which one?

17
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:55,630
It doesn't matter.

18
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:57,810
You can't possibly win.

19
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:58,960
Sheldon, don't ruin the game.

20
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:00,410
How could he ruin the game?

21
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:02,170
Given the cards that have already been played,

22
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:04,760
Penny can only be holding necromancer potions,

23
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:07,090
Which are only effective against wraiths and day-walkers,

24
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:08,820
And there are no more of either left to be drawn.

25
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:10,260
The cards remaining in the undrawn stack are:

26
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:14,610
Four fire weapons, a troll, two ogres and the jewel of osiris.

27
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:16,930
See? Ruined.

28
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,770
Sheldon, that is incredible.

29
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:22,950
From your vantage point, it certainly must seem so.

30
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:26,160
Sheldon has kind of a photographic memory.

31
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:28,280
"photographic" is a misnomer.

32
00:01:28,330 --> 00:01:31,160
I have an eidetic memory, as I've told you many times.

33
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:33,360
Most recently last year during lunch

34
00:01:33,450 --> 00:01:35,150
On the afternoon of may seventh.

35
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:38,790
You had turkey and complained it was dry.

36
00:01:38,850 --> 00:01:40,620
Well, I guess game'over.

37
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:42,590
Really? Oh, great.

38
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:46,090
I mean, aw.

39
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:49,010
- Okay, I gotta go. - Why?

40
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,550
Because the last me I didn't go,

41
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:53,380
I ended up playing "mystic warlords of ka."

42
00:01:53,470 --> 00:01:56,150
Not "ka. Ka-ah."

43
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,360
Buh-eye.

44
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,440
See ya.

45
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:04,190
Still can't believe she's going out with me.

46
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,950
Nobody can.

47
00:02:07,370 --> 00:02:09,820
That reminds me I have a bone to pick with you.

48
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:10,570
What?

49
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:12,520
You and I made a pact

50
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:14,990
That if either of us ever got a hot girlfriend,

51
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,490
That person would have his girlfriend

52
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:19,710
Hook the other guy up with one of her girlfriends.

53
00:02:19,790 --> 00:02:21,750
I don't remember that.

54
00:02:21,830 --> 00:02:24,150
June 30th, 2004.

55
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:27,700
Opening day of Spider-Man 2 at the Amc Pasadena.

56
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:31,410
They only had red icees, no blue.

57
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:32,840
Oh, yeah.

58
00:02:32,890 --> 00:02:35,480
So you've been with Penny for like a month and a half now.

59
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,990
Where's my shorty, morty?

60
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:40,510
Howard, you can't hold me to that.

61
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:41,730
Why not?

62
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,100
Because when I made that agreement,

63
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:44,900
I didn't think I'd ever have a hot girlfriend.

64
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:46,320
And I was positive you ever would.

65
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:50,240
Hey, how come I wasn't part of this deal?

66
00:02:50,330 --> 00:02:52,020
You had left the refreshment stand

67
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:55,530
In order to indulge in your customary preemptive pre-show urination.

68
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:57,410
Oh, so that's how it works?

69
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:00,900
I have a teeny bladder and I don't get a hot girlfriend?

70
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:04,040
Yeah, Raj. That's how it works.

71
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:06,590
Damn.

72
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:36,000
Can I have a napkin?

73
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:38,720
I'm sorry, no.

74
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:41,220
But you have whole bunch of 'em.

75
00:03:41,290 --> 00:03:44,760
Yes, I've moved to a four-napkin system.

76
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:48,430
Lap, hands, face and personal emergency.

77
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,630
If you like, starting tomorrow,

78
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,270
I'll add a guest napkin,

79
00:03:53,350 --> 00:03:56,260
But I'm afraid there's nothing I can do for you today.

80
00:03:59,390 --> 00:04:01,930
Good luck. That's the face napkin.

81
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:04,880
So, have you talked to Penny yet?

82
00:04:04,950 --> 00:04:06,030
No, I haven't.

83
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,170
Why not?

84
00:04:07,170 --> 00:04:08,550
Because I've been busy,

85
00:04:08,550 --> 00:04:10,370
Because I haven't figured out a way to bring it up,

86
00:04:10,370 --> 00:04:13,350
And mostly-- and I can't stress how key this is--

87
00:04:13,350 --> 00:04:15,190
Because I don't want to.

88
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:17,510
Leonard, pact is a pact.

89
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:19,550
You have to get Penny to fix me up.

90
00:04:19,630 --> 00:04:20,550
It's not that simple.

91
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:21,720
What am I supposed to say?

92
00:04:21,770 --> 00:04:22,930
"Penny, do you have any friend

93
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:24,380
You'd like to never hear from again?"

94
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:26,600
Come on, I'm smart,

95
00:04:26,690 --> 00:04:31,090
I have good job and I have only three percent body fat.

96
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:32,310
It's true.

97
00:04:32,390 --> 00:04:33,890
I've seen him at the beach.

98
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:36,110
He's like a human chicken wing.

99
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,730
Leonard, come on.

100
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:39,900
Fine. I'll ask if she has a friend for you.

101
00:04:39,950 --> 00:04:41,070
Hot friend.

102
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,040
- Right. - And tall.

103
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:44,790
I want our kids to be able to Ride Space Mountain

104
00:04:44,790 --> 00:04:46,760
Before they're 20.

105
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:49,140
I'll see what I can do.

106
00:04:49,210 --> 00:04:51,260
Hey, Sheldon, guess what I heard today?

107
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:54,380
I'd imagine you heard many number of things today.

108
00:04:54,450 --> 00:04:56,550
When you arrived at work you undoubtedly heard, "hello, Raj.

109
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:57,770
"How are you, Raj?"

110
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,600
Given that you're wearing a new sweater-vest,

111
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:03,920
And possibly, though far less likely, "nice sweater-vest."

112
00:05:03,990 --> 00:05:07,440
Why don't I just tell you what I heard today.

113
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:10,260
That would probably save us some time.

114
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,600
Saturday night at the comic book store,

115
00:05:12,650 --> 00:05:14,280
They're having a "Mystic Warlords of Ka-Ah" tournament.

116
00:05:14,350 --> 00:05:16,770
First prize is $500.

117
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,660
If we team up, we'd be unstoppable.

118
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:20,570
I'm sorry, Raj, but I have no interest

119
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:22,940
In playing a game in which I find no challenge.

120
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:24,480
What about the money?

121
00:05:24,570 --> 00:05:25,590
I have money.

122
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:27,320
This is other money.

123
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:29,770
How does it differ from the money I have?

124
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:32,010
Half of it will be mine.

125
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:35,430
Do you need it to buy a less disturbing sweater-vest?

126
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:38,830
Leonard, help.

127
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,750
Are you kidding?

128
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:44,040
I couldn't even talk him into giving one of his freakin' napkins.

129
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:51,810
Wow, you really are a genius.

130
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,430
Not really.

131
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:55,520
I googled how to do that.

132
00:06:00,490 --> 00:06:05,170
So, listen...Have you ever made a pact with someone?

133
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,010
You mean like a pinky swear?

134
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:11,160
Okay, fine, like a pinky swear.

135
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:13,780
Well, in the first grade, my friend Rosie and I

136
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:15,620
Made a pact to marry Bert and Ernie.

137
00:06:15,670 --> 00:06:18,290
You know, from Sesame street?

138
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,990
I'm familiar with Bert and Ernie.

139
00:06:20,340 --> 00:06:21,990
Then we find out we both wanted Ernie.

140
00:06:23,010 --> 00:06:25,730
We didn't speak again until middle school.

141
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,510
Over puppets?

142
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:30,870
The heart wants what the heart wants, Leonard.

143
00:06:30,930 --> 00:06:32,120
Okay.

144
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:35,140
Speaking of what the heart want-

145
00:06:35,190 --> 00:06:37,760
Um, a long time ago,

146
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:41,410
I made a pact with Wolowitz that kind of involves you.

147
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:53,660
Okay, I don't know where you're going with this,

148
00:06:53,710 --> 00:06:58,690
But tread carefully because it may be the last conversation we ever have.

149
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:01,050
No, no, nothing like that.

150
00:07:01,130 --> 00:07:03,920
The deal was that if either of us ever got a girlfriend,

151
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,200
We'd have her fix the other one up

152
00:07:06,250 --> 00:07:08,020
With one of her friends.

153
00:07:07,950 --> 00:07:11,520
And you thought it's a good time to bring this up right after sex?

154
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:16,330
Well, I sure as hell wasn't going to bring it up before sex.

155
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:21,480
And during, I was trying to remember what I read on google, so...

156
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:27,240
I'm not hooking Wolowitz up with one of my friends.

157
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:30,280
It doesn't have to be a good friend.

158
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:34,510
And you know that deep down inside, Howard's a really nice guy.

159
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:37,280
The problem isn't what's on the inside.

160
00:07:37,370 --> 00:07:39,540
It's the creepy candy coating.

161
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:43,210
Will you at least think about it?

162
00:07:43,270 --> 00:07:45,440
Just as a favor to me?

163
00:07:45,510 --> 00:07:49,260
Oh, great thing about ernie,

164
00:07:49,350 --> 00:07:52,050
Was he never asked me for anything.

165
00:07:52,150 --> 00:07:55,500
He just gave.

166
00:07:56,870 --> 00:08:02,100
Got it. Got it. Got it. Got it. Got it. Got it.

167
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,900
Betty and Veronica?

168
00:08:06,690 --> 00:08:09,420
Hey, Sheldon, the new Greelantern figurine's coming in tomorrow.

169
00:08:09,510 --> 00:08:10,710
Want me to set one aside for you?

170
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,080
Thank you.

171
00:08:12,130 --> 00:08:15,910
You just robbed me of the opportunity to stumble upon the figurine

172
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:17,680
And make the oh-so-satisfying journey

173
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:19,220
From discovery to desire to possession.

174
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:21,480
All right, I won't set one aside for you.

175
00:08:21,550 --> 00:08:22,700
But I must have it.

176
00:08:22,770 --> 00:08:25,210
- Okay, I'll set one aside for you. - Thank you.

177
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:27,220
You know, I can buy all these things online.

178
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:29,580
I come here for the personal service.

179
00:08:32,930 --> 00:08:34,600
Hey, Stuart, is the Wil Wheaton signed up

180
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:35,630
For the Mystic Warlords tournament

181
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:38,230
The Wil Wheaton from Star Trek?

182
00:08:38,290 --> 00:08:40,470
Yeah, he lives around here. Big gamer.

183
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:41,890
Excuse me.

184
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:45,730
Are you saying that wil wheaton aka Ensign Wesley Crusher

185
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:47,640
On Star Trek: The next generation

186
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:49,560
Is going to be participating in your tournament?

187
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:53,920
Oh, I'm sorry, did I rob you of the opportunity to stumble onto that for yourself?

188
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,150
You don't understand.

189
00:08:55,220 --> 00:08:58,810
Growing up, I idolizedle Wil Wheaton.

190
00:08:58,890 --> 00:09:02,660
Wesley Crusher had an eidetic memory just like me.

191
00:09:02,730 --> 00:09:03,790
Ooh, what a coincidence.

192
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,600
Maybe you can discuss with him while you're playing in the tournament.

193
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:08,770
- Sign here. - I was such a fan

194
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:12,190
That in 1995, I traveled ten hours by bus

195
00:09:12,270 --> 00:09:14,400
To a sci-fi convention in Jackson, Mississippi,

196
00:09:14,470 --> 00:09:16,610
Wearing my Starfleet Academy cadet uniform

197
00:09:16,670 --> 00:09:18,490
In order to meet Wil Wheaton

198
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:19,910
And get him to autograph

199
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:22,280
My mint in-package Wesley Crusher action figure

200
00:09:22,350 --> 00:09:25,200
Ooh, it'll be like a reunion then.

201
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:26,250
Sign here.

202
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:29,490
My arduous journey, however, was for naught.

203
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:32,170
Although advertised to appear, he did not show up.

204
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:35,480
It was at that moment, I vowed eternal hatred for Wil Wheaton.

205
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:37,930
Okay, great, you can tell him you hate him.

206
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,230
Sign here.

207
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:42,270
It might also interest you to know that Wil Wheaton

208
00:09:42,330 --> 00:09:45,050
Currently ranks sixth on my all-time enemies list--

209
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:47,050
Right between director Joel Schumacher,

210
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,060
Who nearly destroyed the batman movie franchise,

211
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:51,020
And Billy Sparks,

212
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:52,680
Who lived down the street from me

213
00:09:52,730 --> 00:09:54,810
And put dog poop on the handles of my bicycle.

214
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:56,860
Okay, I get it. He's a bad guy.

215
00:09:56,950 --> 00:09:58,080
Sign here.

216
00:09:58,150 --> 00:10:00,320
In the words of Khan Noonien Singh

217
00:10:00,370 --> 00:10:03,740
In the immortal Wrath of Khan, "he tasks me."

218
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:06,690
He tasks me and I shall have him."

219
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:08,660
No doubt, sign here.

220
00:10:08,710 --> 00:10:11,360
From hell's heart, I stab at thee."

221
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:16,830
All right, raj, looks like you're teamed up

222
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:19,420
With "die, Wil Wheaton, die."

223
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:28,320
So, tell me more about the future mother of my children.

224
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,080
She's adorable, howard.

225
00:10:31,150 --> 00:10:32,400
I think you'll like her.

226
00:10:32,470 --> 00:10:33,620
Great.

227
00:10:33,670 --> 00:10:35,510
So what did you tell her about me?

228
00:10:35,590 --> 00:10:36,960
Did you mention the body fat?

229
00:10:37,030 --> 00:10:40,340
No, I thought that would be a nice surprise for her.

230
00:10:40,430 --> 00:10:43,160
Good, good.

231
00:10:45,430 --> 00:10:48,140
I just told her y're an aerospace engineer,

232
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:49,600
You speak five languages--

233
00:10:49,670 --> 00:10:51,300
Six if you count klingon.

234
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:54,090
Girls don't count klingon, Howard.

235
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:54,860
Right?

236
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:55,980
Right.

237
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,010
Oh. And I told her you have

238
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:00,280
An unhealthy attachment to your mother.

239
00:11:00,350 --> 00:11:01,950
What?

240
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:03,400
I'm kidding.

241
00:11:04,870 --> 00:11:07,350
Another delightful surprise for her.

242
00:11:12,530 --> 00:11:14,380
Sheldon, it's your play.

243
00:11:14,450 --> 00:11:16,530
Sheldon.

244
00:11:18,030 --> 00:11:20,870
My enchanted troll bludgeons your screaming harpy

245
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:22,390
With a cursed mace. Game

246
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:25,090
Sorry, boys.

247
00:11:25,170 --> 00:11:27,890
Say hi to your mother when she picks you up.

248
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:30,560
Or I could just tell her later tonight!

249
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:34,480
We pwned them, dude! Up top!

250
00:11:34,550 --> 00:11:36,070
Look at him.

251
00:11:36,150 --> 00:11:40,520
Wil Wheaton, my old friend.

252
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:42,990
I have chased you 'round the moons of Nibia

253
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:47,360
And 'round the Antares Maelstrom and 'round perdition's ames!

254
00:11:47,430 --> 00:11:49,700
You know, you keep quoting wrath of Khan,

255
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:50,980
But he was in next generation.

256
00:11:51,050 --> 00:11:52,920
It's a totally different set of characters.

257
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,450
Silence!

258
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:58,420
How much longer must I wait for my revenge?

259
00:11:58,510 --> 00:12:00,390
Well, if Wil Wheaton and Stuart win their match

260
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:03,040
And we beat Lonely Larry and Captain Sweatpants

261
00:12:03,090 --> 00:12:04,260
In the next round,

262
00:12:04,350 --> 00:12:06,250
We'll face off for the championship.

263
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:09,580
So, my path to satisfaction is blocked

264
00:12:09,630 --> 00:12:12,990
By Lonely Larry and Captain Sweatpants.

265
00:12:13,050 --> 00:12:15,320
Very well.

266
00:12:15,390 --> 00:12:17,910
They must be destroyed.

267
00:12:17,980 --> 00:12:20,060
Dude, you have to stop talking like that.

268
00:12:20,110 --> 00:12:21,140
It's really lame.

269
00:12:21,230 --> 00:12:23,660
Silence!

270
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:31,520
So, Penny tells me you're working as a waitress

271
00:12:31,610 --> 00:12:33,440
To put yourself through grade school.

272
00:12:33,510 --> 00:12:35,560
That's pretty great. What are you studying?

273
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:36,660
Microbiology.

274
00:12:36,730 --> 00:12:41,530
Oh, cool. So you could study me.

275
00:12:41,620 --> 00:12:43,530
I don'understand.

276
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:48,190
Microbiology is the study of tiny living things.

277
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:51,370
I know, I'm studying it.

278
00:12:51,380 --> 00:12:58,330
And I said you could study me 'cause I'm a tiny living thing.

279
00:12:58,380 --> 00:13:01,030
It's a joke.

280
00:13:01,090 --> 00:13:03,090
Are you sure?

281
00:13:07,730 --> 00:13:08,840
Do you like Sic-Fiction?

282
00:13:08,890 --> 00:13:09,840
No.

283
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:11,010
Role-playing games?

284
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:14,010
Like in the bedroom or like Dungeons and Dragons?

285
00:13:14,060 --> 00:13:15,550
Either.

286
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,400
No.

287
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:21,240
Gonna be a long night.

288
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,940
Well, it's your fault.

289
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:26,680
I had to ask. You didn't have to say yes.

290
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,910
You like magic?

291
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,910
Not really.

292
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,560
Okay.

293
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,560
Long-long night.

294
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:44,260
I play my endless serpent. Raj will play ecstatic frenzy,

295
00:13:44,350 --> 00:13:46,230
which means Larry will have to play Chaos Overlord.

296
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:48,300
Then Captain Sweatpants, Molten River.

297
00:13:48,380 --> 00:13:51,100
I play nightshade dryad. Game, set and match.

298
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:58,110
Now fetch me Wil Wheaton!

299
00:13:59,590 --> 00:14:04,610
Bot-tash bir jab-loo-di rekh kkhakkh-o ny!

300
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:07,230
Did that guy just say

301
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:10,370
"revenge is a dish best served cold" in Klingon?

302
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:12,720
I believe so.

303
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:16,330
What is wrong with him?

304
00:14:16,410 --> 00:14:19,210
Everyone has a different theory.

305
00:14:23,050 --> 00:14:25,250
How about computers?

306
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,590
Do you like computers?

307
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:29,470
I use them. I don't like them.

308
00:14:29,470 --> 00:14:32,120
Okay...

309
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:35,330
Puppets?  Where do you stand on puppies?.

310
00:14:35,430 --> 00:14:38,650
A puppy once bit my face.

311
00:14:38,730 --> 00:14:40,270
Of course it did.

312
00:14:40,330 --> 00:14:42,770
How about that? Einstein was wrong.

313
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:43,600
What?

314
00:14:43,650 --> 00:14:44,850
Approaching the speed of light

315
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:45,940
Doesn't slow down time.

316
00:14:45,990 --> 00:14:47,190
Approaching them does.

317
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,360
Excuse me.

318
00:14:52,450 --> 00:14:54,200
Oh, damn. It's my mother.

319
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:55,480
Are you going to answer it?

320
00:14:55,530 --> 00:14:56,520
I'm torn

321
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:58,650
She might be dying, and, you know,

322
00:14:58,720 --> 00:14:59,990
I wouldn't want to miss that.

323
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,310
On the other hand,

324
00:15:02,370 --> 00:15:07,530
If I let it go to voicemail, I could play it over and over.

325
00:15:07,590 --> 00:15:11,880
I know how you feel. My mother makes me crazy.

326
00:15:11,970 --> 00:15:14,630
Not as crazy as my mother makes me.

327
00:15:14,690 --> 00:15:15,840
Oh, yeah?

328
00:15:15,890 --> 00:15:17,520
Does your mother call u every day at work

329
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:19,020
To see if you've had a healthy lunch?

330
00:15:19,110 --> 00:15:20,960
My mother calls me at work

331
00:15:21,030 --> 00:15:23,680
To see if I had a healthy bowel movement.

332
00:15:27,530 --> 00:15:31,120
Does she lay out your clothes for you in the morning

333
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,400
Like you're nine years old?

334
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:34,470
You live with your mother?

335
00:15:34,540 --> 00:15:36,710
No. That's the sad part.

336
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:38,790
Ooh, rough.

337
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,160
Okay, check this out.

338
00:15:40,210 --> 00:15:42,330
My mother made me we rubber gloves to kindergarten

339
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:46,220
So I wouldn't pick up a disease from the other children.

340
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:47,580
That's nothing.

341
00:15:47,670 --> 00:15:48,850
I couldn't ride a bicle

342
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:52,220
'cause my mother was afraid I'd hit a bump and lose my virginity.

343
00:15:54,560 --> 00:15:55,590
You didn't, did you?

344
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:57,310
Not on a bicle.

345
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:59,260
In a Camry.

346
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:03,330
Corolla!

347
00:16:04,750 --> 00:16:06,440
- More wine? - I'd love some.

348
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:10,110
Listen, you have to come to Shabbat dinner at my house sometime.

349
00:16:10,190 --> 00:16:11,320
Why?

350
00:16:11,390 --> 00:16:14,360
A catholic girl like you, wearing a big cross like that

351
00:16:14,410 --> 00:16:17,000
Might just give my mother the big brain aneurysm

352
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:18,230
I've been hoping for.

353
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:23,120
Okay, but only if you come

354
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:25,590
To Sunday dinner at my house wearing a yarmulke.

355
00:16:25,590 --> 00:16:26,940
It's a date.

356
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:30,490
Am I a matchmaker or what?

357
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,900
Lava Serpent.

358
00:16:38,990 --> 00:16:42,870
Nest of snakes.

359
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:43,910
Underworld Guardian.

360
00:16:43,990 --> 00:16:45,790
Underworld Guardian.

361
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:48,910
We skirmish to the death.

362
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:55,530
Invisibility Spell.

363
00:16:55,590 --> 00:16:56,850
Luminescence Spell.

364
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:58,000
Water Nymph.

365
00:16:58,050 --> 00:16:59,020
Fire Demon.

366
00:16:59,090 --> 00:17:00,370
Two-headed Tiger.

367
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:02,220
Three-headed Lion.

368
00:17:02,310 --> 00:17:04,090
Sulphur.

369
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:05,380
Brimstone.

370
00:17:07,430 --> 00:17:09,600
Problem, Wil Wheaton?

371
00:17:12,130 --> 00:17:13,130
Hang on.

372
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:15,550
You're holding two Moderate Spell cards,

373
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:17,590
A Small Rock and a Potion of Zancor

374
00:17:17,590 --> 00:17:19,310
Which will be about as much help

375
00:17:19,310 --> 00:17:21,040
As an air conditioner on the ice planet Hoth.

376
00:17:21,110 --> 00:17:23,310
Your only move is to play the Potion,

377
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,000
Lose the skirmish,

378
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,130
And two moves later, the game.

379
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:29,950
I think he's got me.

380
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:34,820
The year was 1995.

381
00:17:34,910 --> 00:17:37,530
The place: Jackson, Mississippi.

382
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:40,200
Having spent ten hours on a bus,

383
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:42,120
During which I had to twice violate my personal rule

384
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:46,510
Against relieving myself on board a moving vehicle...

385
00:17:47,810 --> 00:17:48,960
I finally arrived

386
00:17:49,020 --> 00:17:51,740
At the fourth annual Dixie-Trek convention

387
00:17:51,830 --> 00:17:56,250
Only to find that my idol Wil Wheaton decided he had

388
00:17:56,330 --> 00:17:59,870
Better things to do than to show up and sign my Action Figure.

389
00:18:03,890 --> 00:18:05,210
What?

390
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:09,060
You betrayed me, Wil Wheaton.

391
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:13,600
Now I have my revenge.

392
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:18,400
You went to the '95 Dixie-Trek?

393
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,910
Oh, dude, my grandmother had just died,

394
00:18:22,990 --> 00:18:25,390
And I had to go to her funeral.

395
00:18:27,830 --> 00:18:30,270
Your mee-maw died?

396
00:18:32,250 --> 00:18:33,470
That's terrible.

397
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:35,450
Yeah, it was.

398
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:38,960
But I'm really sorry that I disappointed you.

399
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:41,880
No, no, I understand.

400
00:18:41,930 --> 00:18:43,510
Anything happened to my mee-maw,

401
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:45,580
I'd be one inconsolable moon pie.

402
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:48,920
I should clarify that statement

403
00:18:48,970 --> 00:18:51,970
By explaining that she calls me "moon pie."

404
00:18:52,040 --> 00:18:54,590
It'a special relationship, isn't it,

405
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,390
Between a boy and his grandmother?

406
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:57,960
Oh, yes.

407
00:18:58,030 --> 00:19:00,930
Okay, great, everybody loves their grandmas!

408
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:03,720
Now, come on, Sheldon, finish him off!

409
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:05,400
It's okay, Sheldon.

410
00:19:05,450 --> 00:19:06,540
I let you down.

411
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:08,270
I deserve it.

412
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:09,910
Potion of Zancor.

413
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:15,460
What are you waiting for?!

414
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:17,210
Kill Wil Wheaton!

415
00:19:17,250 --> 00:19:19,560
From Hell's Heart, stab at him!

416
00:19:21,430 --> 00:19:23,890
I can't.

417
00:19:23,950 --> 00:19:26,250
Sure you can. Do it! Do it!

418
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:28,790
No.

419
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:31,130
I came here to defeat Wil Wheaton,

420
00:19:31,230 --> 00:19:33,850
The man who destroyed my dreams.

421
00:19:33,930 --> 00:19:39,650
But I can't defeat Wil Wheaton,the man who loved his mee-maw.

422
00:19:42,190 --> 00:19:44,440
Enchanted Bunny.

423
00:19:44,490 --> 00:19:48,830
No! Not Enchanted Bunny!

424
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:52,280
I call my mee-maw "Nana."

425
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:55,580
And she's going be very happy

426
00:19:55,650 --> 00:19:58,920
To hear that my Small Rock kills your Enchanted Bunny.

427
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:03,680
Game over, moon pie.

428
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:08,500
I-I-I don't understand.

429
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:10,770
Your grandmother's alive?

430
00:20:10,830 --> 00:20:12,430
Oh, you catch on quick.

431
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:15,850
Come on, Stewie, let's get our prize money.

432
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:20,280
That was fun.

433
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:30,350
Wheaton!

434
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:33,920
Wheaton! Wheaton!

